@zachleat So, to be clear: you are still building 474 open graph *images*, you're just not building 474 separate static HTML pages just to screenshot them to make the images. 

You're using the Chromium-based screenshot service as the build tool instead of using eleventy plus also the screenshot service.

That seems like a sensible use of resources. But its not quite as impressive as you implied yesterday; your total build time including the screenshots is still proportional to page count.

