@iamdtms 
Nice! In 2022, putting the dots on their own aria-hidden element was a good improvement. These days, it's no longer necessary (depending on your level of support for older browsers), `content` can have alternative text, including `""` for decorative content.

https://codepen.io/ccwilcox/pen/MYpJrYg?editors=1100
@zachleat

@iamdtms 
I was just pointing out an option available now that avoids adding unnecessary HTML elements and uses less code overall.

Yours is forked from a version that had the pseudo-elements attached to `<span class="title">`. Yours had them attached to an added element, `<span class="leaders" aria-hidden="true"></span>`. The only reason to make that change is to prevent the dots from being read by screen readers.
My fork goes back to attaching them to `.title` and using `/ ""` within the `content` to prevent the dots from being read by screen readers.
